    "message": "feat(websearch): forward extracted content, domain filters, and real error codes\n\nThree gaps between what the web search stack fetches and what Claude actually\nreceives.\n\nExtracted page content was discarded. Seven adapters populate\nWebSearchResultItem.content and the digest already read it, but\n_web_search_response_items never copied it across -- so EXA_CONTENTS,\nTAVILY_INCLUDE_RAW_CONTENT and FIRECRAWL_SCRAPE_FORMAT were switchable in the\nadmin UI, billed by the provider, rendered in the analytics detail modal, and\ninvisible to the model. Content now reaches the digest and is preferred over the\nsnippet under its own WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS cap (default 2000), so\nopting into it is not trimmed back to snippet length.\n\nDomain filters never left the API layer. registry.search, every adapter, and the\nanalytics input payload already accepted allowed_domains/blocked_domains, but\nnothing read them off the client's tool definition, leaving SUPPORTS_DOMAINS\ndead in production on five providers. Anthropic declares them on the tool rather\nthan the tool call, where they arrive as extras on Tool; they are now read and\nforwarded, and the per-attempt record shows the real values instead of a\nhardcoded empty list. max_uses is honoured to the extent this single-shot path\ncan. Requests carrying both lists resolve to the allow list rather than silently\nintersecting, matching Anthropic's rejection of that combination.\n\nEvery failure reported error_code \"unavailable\". Anthropic documents six, and a\nclient acts on the difference: too_many_requests is worth retrying, an invalid\ninput never is. Rate-limit and quota failures now map to too_many_requests,\nrejected requests to invalid_tool_input, an exhausted budget to\nmax_uses_exceeded; anything not confidently classifiable stays unavailable.\n\nVerification: new tests cover content passthrough and digest preference, tool\noption parsing including the both-lists case, end-to-end forwarding into\nsearch_with_logging, and the error-code table. Existing digest-shape\nexpectations updated for the additive content key. Full suite passes except 14\nfailures that also fail on unmodified main -- 8 from real API keys in the local\nenvironment defeating test isolation, 6 from the PowerShell installer tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
